The prime factorization of $403$ is $13 \cdot 31$. Therefore, either $a+5 = 13$ and $b - 6 = 31$ or $a + 5 = 31$ and $b - 6 = 13$.  \begin{eqnarray} \mbox{In the former case, we have } a = 8 \mbox{ and } b = 37, \mbox{ and } |a-b| = 29.  \end{eqnarray}
\begin{eqnarray} \mbox{In the latter case, we have } a = 26 \mbox{ and } b = 19, \mbox{ and } |a-b| = 7.  \end{eqnarray} Hence, the minimal possible value of $|a-b|$ is $7$.
